# compiler-rt — lift-source

Upstream: https://github.com/conda-forge/compiler-rt-feedstock
Fork:     https://github.com/NAGAGroup/compiler-rt-feedstock
Pinned:   37f9cbf4c2ad977dcfc95a8d1d0ad582a402d589 (conda-forge main, 2026-08-26)

LIFT, NOT SUBMODULE: we do not build this feedstock. Its content is copied
into our own core recipe, because acpp forces LLVM+clang into ONE cmake
configure and conda-forge's per-component split cannot carry it.

The sanitizer/builtins runtime behind our acpp-compiler-rt output. WHAT WE
LIFT: its build flags and install layout — in particular where the runtime
libraries must land relative to the clang resource dir, which is what the
Windows activation's explicit
-Wl,-defaultlib:.../clang_rt.builtins-<arch>.lib depends on.

TO DIFF AGAINST UPSTREAM:
    git clone https://github.com/NAGAGroup/compiler-rt-feedstock
    git -C compiler-rt-feedstock diff 37f9cbf4c2ad977dcfc95a8d1d0ad582a402d589..origin/main
